[I] Display VDPAU capabilities of the running driver

[T] vdpauinfo prints the decoder profiles, surface formats and other
[T] capabilities the installed VDPAU driver exposes. It is the VDPAU
[T] counterpart of vainfo and the usual way to check whether hardware
[T] video decoding is set up correctly.

[U] https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/vdpau/vdpauinfo

[A] VDPAU project
[M] Dennie Mahne <dennie.mahne@gmail.com>

[C] extra/tool

